  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is doing simple harmonic motion of amplitude $0.06 \\mathrm{~m}$ and time period $3.14 \\mathrm{~s}$. The maximum velocity of the particle is _______ $\\mathrm{cm} / \\mathrm{s}$."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{V}_{\\max } & =\\omega \\mathrm{A} \\quad \\text { at mean position } \\\\\n& =\\frac{2 \\pi}{\\mathrm{T}} \\mathrm{A}=\\frac{2 \\pi}{\\pi} \\times 0.06=0.12 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{sec} \\\\\n\\mathrm{V}_{\\max } & =12 \\mathrm{~cm} / \\mathrm{sec}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}